<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Random Team Picker | Split Names Into Groups</title><meta name="description" content="Shuffle a list of names and split them into balanced random teams. Choose the number of teams and instantly generate groups."><meta name="robots" content="index,follow"><link rel="canonical" href="https://wheelnamepicker.com.au/team-picker"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/value-pages.css"></head><body><div class="top"><div class="nav"><a class="brand" href="/">Wheel Name Picker</a><div class="links"><a href="/student-picker">Student Picker</a><a href="/activity-picker">Activity Picker</a><a href="/guides/classroom-fair-picking">Classroom Guide</a></div></div></div><header class="hero"><span class="badge">Group maker</span><h1>Random Team Picker</h1><p>Paste a list of names, choose how many teams you need and generate balanced groups. The list is shuffled first, then distributed across teams one name at a time.</p></header><main class="wrap"><div class="tool"><div class="grid"><div class="field"><label for="names">Names</label><textarea id="names">Alex
Bailey
Charlie
Dakota
Elliot
Frankie
Georgie
Harper</textarea></div><div class="field"><label for="teams">Number of teams</label><input id="teams" type="number" min="2" value="2"><div class="actions"><button id="make">Make teams</button><button class="secondary" id="again">Shuffle again</button></div></div></div><div class="result" id="result">Your teams will appear here.</div></div><div class="article"><section><h2>Balanced random groups in seconds</h2><p>The team picker is designed for situations where you want quick, roughly even groups without manually deciding who goes where. It works for classrooms, workshops, family games, training sessions and casual community activities.</p><p>When the number of people cannot be divided evenly, some teams will contain one extra person. The tool spreads those extras across the first teams rather than putting them all together.</p></section><section><h2>How the shuffle works</h2><p>Before groups are built, the names are shuffled using a standard in-browser randomisation method. The shuffled list is then dealt across the requested number of teams. Re-running the picker reshuffles the whole list, so a new grouping can be created without retyping names.</p></section><section><h2>When random teams work well</h2><ul><li>Short classroom activities where friendship groups are not part of the learning goal.</li><li>Workshop breakout tasks where you want participants to mix.</li><li>Family or party games where balanced numbers matter more than skill level.</li><li>Practice drills where changing partners encourages variety.</li></ul></section><section><h2>When to use something other than random</h2><p>Random grouping is not always the best choice. If teams need balanced skill levels, accessibility support, language pairing or carefully managed social dynamics, deliberate teacher or facilitator grouping may be more appropriate. This tool only randomises the names supplied; it cannot understand those contextual needs.</p></section><section><h2>Tips for smoother group activities</h2><p>Tell participants how long the groups will last, what each team needs to produce and whether roles should be assigned inside each group. If you are using temporary groups, a second random tool such as the <a href="/student-picker">Student Picker</a> can choose a spokesperson or starter after the teams are formed.</p></section></div></main><footer class="footer"><a href="/about">About</a><a href="/privacy">Privacy</a><a href="/terms">Terms</a><a href="/contact/">Contact</a><p>© 2026 Wheel Name Picker · Ascension Digital Group</p></footer><script>const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);function run(){const names=$('names').value.split(/\n|,/).map(x=>x.trim()).filter(Boolean);let n=Math.floor(Number($('teams').value)||2);if(names.length<2)return $('result').textContent='Add at least two names.';n=Math.max(2,Math.min(n,names.length));for(let i=names.length-1;i>0;i--){const j=Math.floor(Math.random()*(i+1));[names[i],names[j]]=[names[j],names[i]]}const groups=Array.from({length:n},()=>[]);names.forEach((x,i)=>groups[i%n].push(x));$('result').innerHTML='<div class="grid">'+groups.map((g,i)=>`<div class="team"><strong>Team ${i+1}</strong><br>${g.join('<br>')}</div>`).join('')+'</div>'}$('make').onclick=run;$('again').onclick=run;</script></body></html>